-- title:
--   Distinct blow-up ends at a supersingular point are separated
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = \exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be (`hH₁`) the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$ (along $\ell \mid q^2 M'$). Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal (`hK`) to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the subfield generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field of the group [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q^2*M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133).
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation domain with algebraically closed residue field, which is an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ its fraction field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ (`hζA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion (`hj`) the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the $q$-expansion $\mathsf{q}^{-1} + \dots$ of the modular $j$-function. Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`) and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy (`hϖt`) $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$. Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$. Let $y \subset C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), supersingular in the sense (`hss`) that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of elements $j_0$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero affine point killed by $q$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (a Drinfeld-chart presentation with riders, at every supersingular closed point; its seven clauses are named below) states: for every point $z$ of the scheme [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout of the two charts $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j^{-1}$-chart algebra along their common localisation), every element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk at $z$ equal to the germ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, lying in the maximal ideal of that stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` and satisfying the same supersingularity condition (`hss'`) as above with $y$ replaced by $y'$, there exist: a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v - fu)$, such that, writing `toC` for the completion map, `mkS` for the quotient map and `germY` for the germ map $C \to$ stalk at $z$: (i) $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ carries the germ of $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) every automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ over $L$ which is a level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, in the sense of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) (on ratios of $q$-expansions of modular forms of level `GammaH (q^2*M') H₁`, $\tau$ acts through the substitution by the matrix `conjElemN q γ⁻¹`), maps $C$ into $C$; (iii) if moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ is the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) if $\tau$ is as in (ii) and is the identity modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ compatible with $\tau$ through $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$, a scalar $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in \mathrm{Mat}_2(W)$ such that $\theta$ fixes all constants, $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0, X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, $c \equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; (v) prime ideals $P_1, P_2$ of $S$ not containing both classes of $X_0, X_1$, containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, and containing respectively elements $a_1X_0 + b_1X_1 + h_1$ and $a_2X_0 + b_2X_1 + h_2$ with $h_i \in (X_0,X_1)^2$ and $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions along $\mathrm{toC}$ followed by $e$; (vi) for such a prime $P$ containing an element $X_0 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$ and for $a \in C$, the element $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (vii) the series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $j$-expansion with all exponents multiplied by $q$) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and for a suitable $a_0 \in A$ with the difference in $y'$, there are $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\,\cdot\,)))$ equal to the class of $h$, such that for all $a, b \in W$, one of them a unit, with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, the sum $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} (\text{coeff of } X_0^iX_1^{e_0-i} \text{ in } h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit.
--
--   Fix now a point $z$ with data $\varpi_z$ (`hϖz`, `hz`) and $y'$ over $z$ (`hy'`) satisfying the supersingularity condition `hss'`, and assume (`hy'y`) that $y'$ is the ideal $y$. Fix also a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, series $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1 - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ with $S := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for this data exactly the seven clauses (i)–(vii) listed above.
--
--   Let $J$ be the ideal of $C$ given (`hJ`) as the infimum of all ideals of the form $\tau^{-1}$ of the contraction along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$, where $\gamma$ runs over $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ over the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ which preserve $C$. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ given (`hB`) by adjoining to $C$ the set $\{x \in K \mid \exists\, i \in J,\ x\varpi_t = i\}$, and let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). The remaining structural hypotheses are: `hR1` (two clauses) that $C \le B$ and that every element of $K$ is a ratio $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \neq 0$; `hR2` (three clauses) that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) that an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b \in C$ one has $b \in y$ if and only if $b \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, and that $f \in W$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses) that (a) for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the set of $b$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, compatible with $A \to k$, and such that each level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$ acts on the coordinate ring through [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) at some $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), with $c \ne 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; (b) $B$ is stable under all such $\tau$; (c) every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is hit, via some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and corresponding $\tau$, by the centre $\{b \in B : b \in \mathfrak{m}_W\}$; (d) an element of $B$ all of whose translates under such $\gamma, \tau$ lie in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; (e) a level automorphism for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$.
--
--   Finally let $O$ and $O'$ be subrings of $K$ each of which (`hO`, `hO'`) arises as follows: there is $a \in J$ with nonzero image in $K$ such that, setting $B_a$ to be $C$ with $\{x \in K \mid \exists\, i \in J,\ xa = i\}$ adjoined, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with $O$ (resp. $O'$) consisting exactly of the ratios $g/h$ with $g, h \in B_a$ and $h \notin P$, such that every element of $y$ lying in $O$ (resp. $O'$) is a non-unit there, and such that $B$ is not contained in $O$ (resp. $O'$). Assume $O \neq O'$ (`hne`).
--
--   Conclusion: there exists $f \in K$ lying in $O$ and in $O'$ such that $f$ is not a unit of $O$ and $f$ is a unit of $O'$.
--
--   This is the separation step for the ends of the blow-up of the supersingular chart of the integral model: two distinct local rings obtained from charts of the blow-up of $C$ along $J$, both centred at the supersingular point $y$ and neither containing the $\varpi_t$-chart $B$, are distinguished by a single function, a unit at one end and a non-unit at the other. It is used in the counting statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_finset_ends_iff_isLocalization_blowupChart_card_eq_of_eq_adjoin_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_finset_ends_iff_isLocalization_blowupChart_card_eq_of_eq_adjoin_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd), and is the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-diamond form of the argument, valid for all primes $q$.
